        "contentId": "quran_7_96",
        "why": "7:96 ends \"but they denied, so We seized them for what they used to earn\" — its hopeful clause is a counterfactual about people who did not believe, and the complete ayah closes on punishment. Citing only the first half would break the complete-ayah rule, so the verse is swapped rather than cut. 25:74 is a du'a for comfort of the eyes."
      }
